      "content": {
        "value": "This page captures the agreed ways of working for the SFCC Zimmermann delivery teams. It serves as the single reference point for how we work together across both squads, covering our Definition of Ready, Definition of Done.\n\nAll team members — developers, BAs, QEs, and architects — are expected to be familiar with the standards documented here. These are not guidelines — they are the agreed baseline for how stories are refined, built, tested, and delivered on this engagement.\n\nThis page is owned by the Scrum Master and reviewed at the end of each PI. Any proposed changes to ways of working are raised in the Sprint Retrospective and updated here once agreed by the team.\n\n**What you will find here**\n\n* **Definition of Ready** — the criteria a story must meet before it enters sprint planning\n* **Definition of Done** — the criteria a story must meet before it is marked complete",
